{"title":"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(No_Miquel&#39;s_point)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (No Miquel's point)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Sparrow_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Sparrow solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Step_1:_Establishing_the_Initial_Relation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 1: Establishing the Initial Relation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Step_2:_Tracking_Angles_Subtended_by_Arcs_of_Circle\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 2: Tracking Angles Subtended by Arcs of Circle</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Step_3:_Proving_Quadrilateral_is_Cyclic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 3: Proving Quadrilateral  is Cyclic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Step_4:_Proving_Quadrilateral_is_Cyclic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 4: Proving Quadrilateral  is Cyclic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Step_5:_Final_Evaluation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Step 5: Final Evaluation</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> passes through the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> again at distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of intersection of the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1590a6dd5bd44d78ef74b499874afebfd3ac4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KBN$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> (apart from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />). Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9063f273653119f7fd7d25519993eb166e4f94b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMB = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the Miquel Point of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/16817764491379f69247eae98099a6a886a6a8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACNK$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, so there is a spiral similarity centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> that takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b902cd5392b3e4bbda5878d8ae7f99eb8291eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KN$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a4a0680d4e0668219585d856c7f109cd09f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da106a1676da5205f5c12c490b671acb3e63a490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KA$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c879631d01bcc51ec112e4a32a039f624d40c91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1541c81fa3dd8b6dac74fda5597d1cdb6e662d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />. Thus the spiral similarity must also send <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a4a0680d4e0668219585d856c7f109cd09f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c879631d01bcc51ec112e4a32a039f624d40c91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db8653d45714d9350dc36eb7d88a68e3be49628f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMM_1 M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> is cyclic. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d6f4df5fdccfa8f3ccb1c37f550041a9540581f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM_1 B M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> is also cyclic with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac69127bb7a97d71d1cf903e964140436bea116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> must lie on the same circumcircle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a4a0680d4e0668219585d856c7f109cd09f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c879631d01bcc51ec112e4a32a039f624d40c91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9063f273653119f7fd7d25519993eb166e4f94b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMB = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1985_IMO.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/34/1985_IMO.png/450px-1985_IMO.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"344\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/34/1985_IMO.png/675px-1985_IMO.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/34/1985_IMO.png/900px-1985_IMO.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/770df7496f6ecbc0404c281f6be0c52742ad04d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega, \\Omega&#39;, \\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2660647e04cab6b0f48366f94d0a38303c5d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O,O&#39;,O&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"19\" /> be the circumcircles and circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b0319691c1fc508fb2ada031be5f2c50032c9ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKNC, ABC, BNKM,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/721ce05291690961f7e72293fc80219fa44c3cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = \\gamma, AKNC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be38f1c3a60cdc760d2112a5d73659c8f1f0ba51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle BKN = \\gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/452004df93ffbd564aa04b47a54afa6c3b7a5984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO&#39;&#39; = BO&#39;&#39; = \\frac {BN}{2 \\sin \\gamma}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"187\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1541c81fa3dd8b6dac74fda5597d1cdb6e662d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> respectively.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590f7f52f8992f134f749e453a378b297bac233f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE \\perp BC, OD \\perp BC, OO&#39; \\perp AC, DE = \\frac {BC}{2} - \\frac {NC}{2} = \\frac {BN}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"478\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc2c86b82c396cb27dde075ff2b81514c50cc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies OO&#39; = \\frac {DE}{\\sin \\gamma} = \\frac {BN}{2 \\sin \\gamma} = MO&#39;&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"292\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the Miquel Point of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbde29f221872561c23e7bd2629ed08f983ce173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACNK,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> so  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52af35157c201fda7e448cfccf58b654c1140e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO&#39;&#39;O&#39;O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> is cyclic.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52af35157c201fda7e448cfccf58b654c1140e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO&#39;&#39;O&#39;O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> is trapezium <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b150238aa280f1594a8522fb0b388ba463b6a25d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies O&#39;&#39;O&#39; || MO.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5bfb01d0dfc177e5a3ff86eea42bc993b8f86e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O&#39;&#39;O&#39; \\perp BM \\implies MO\\perp BM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"244\" height=\"16\" /> as desired. \n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28No_Miquel.27s_point.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(No_Miquel's_point)\">Solution 3 (No Miquel's point)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (No Miquel&#39;s point)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc01ccef46950bd7abeeb47009bf021bd35ed115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MKA$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44acca8281d071a67876a873212b43334621033c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MNC$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, they are similar because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c745f86facc5ac8171930f1a676d40aefb7ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MAK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c89291f0fe27b92a815b6d3cb16827e3d2627f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MCN$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3527722133e39b32b96fdebeb299e2dd5890b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MKA = \\angle MNC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35b19db53c4382abe9bff4f53565c9c5eaad2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP \\perp AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46f61ac078c76280916f1e863eb64c956ab2576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Naturally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370334b1a3582d54fad42c735dfdded7d216d3cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba369b33271c6fb52789f86292cc68559a2e0411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e42c53cdd80df076ce76603fdb3d96e5b57657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MAP \\sim \\triangle MCQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />, because \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9dadecc862ccc94b60020c394a0496280038c116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AP}{CQ} = \\frac {AK}{CN} = \\frac {AM}{CB}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"160\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b6cec2870ed32dec3cd0095106b60a3249e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMP = \\angle CMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219cdb1901ee76dfdd02a64590dd69052454fb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PMQ = \\angle AMC = \\angle ABC = \\angle PBQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"308\" height=\"18\" />. Obviously BMPQ is cyclic, and so is BPOQ. Finally, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eee315868ec218866e31dbf7eb462641e39604d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM \\perp MB$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. (<b>by gougutheorem</b>)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Sparrow_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Sparrow_solution)\">Solution 4 (Sparrow solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Sparrow solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ae/IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png/300px-IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"206\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ae/IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png/450px-IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ae/IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png/600px-IMO_1985_5_Sparrow.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67ca379b8d2ac757c4b9de50138d75cef8485220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega,Q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8dcf98ed1b21dbc446aa28d097d4281599c25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> circumcenter and radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec139772967f5bc10790d88971378b3f2167efec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,O&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/09129ffbb633d02cac8500ce3b57817ddb441579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle KBN,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> circumcenter and radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175b406f7711cc41b32454cf27168506703aecde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BO&#39; = MO&#39; = r, BQ = MQ = R \\implies\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/3313d022577663da72650b768c8d6bd9e37cb217.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[QO&#39; \\perp MB, \\angle BQO&#39;  = \\angle MQO&#39;.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b9f3accb8cef1c55bb4ba5220fde760a8eadbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKNC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b902cd5392b3e4bbda5878d8ae7f99eb8291eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KN$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is antiparallel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa10fa91d9731d1fc2f16c9443b675a462ca46a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC, O&#39;O \\perp KN.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sparrow%E2%80%99s_lemmas\" title=\"Sparrow’s lemmas\"> Sparrow’s Lemma 3A</a> for circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and get that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f2d56588b9482ec9e17dc73757691f883f6cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49bb8cb1ec49d8cb2e97175f0b905b7ade9a0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\implies BO&#39; \\perp AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95fbfb49b675ba11392ba7c2603d0c87f89be76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bf1515283dbd146b76682d75b2ebb84d8a0214f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is isogonal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b544762d421643e13f448b9fa36eb9cd8204597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO&#39; \\implies OO&#39; || BQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> lies on bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f57114563a98bd42acda9525e4bb528d7e1e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\implies BO&#39; || QO \\implies BO&#39;OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" /> is parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610493b6521deb12789365a542562169e4146367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies OO&#39; = BQ = R, BO&#39; = QO = r = O&#39;D \\implies DO&#39;QO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"471\" height=\"19\" /> is parallelogram.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f125220018d711be954ce797ba4aa4b91554cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BO&#39;M = 2 \\varphi \\implies \\angle O&#39;MD = \\angle O&#39;DM = \\varphi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330c9cc1ed9095bd756dad6c51e487d856556e1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle DO&#39;Q = 180^\\circ - \\varphi - (180^\\circ - 2 \\varphi) = \\varphi \\implies MD || O&#39;Q \\perp MB \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"18\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is my synthetic solution for <b>IMO 1985 Problem 5</b> without relying on Miquel's Theorem, using pure angle chasing and cyclic quadrilaterals.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_Statement\">Problem Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> passes through the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> again at distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. The circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868874d27f0612c79debb5cd8e33bdca03d35f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle KBN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at exactly two distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb796b3a4c9c4ccc9c3f93bc14aee6ee419004a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMB = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO1985_Problem5.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9b/IMO1985_Problem5.jpg/750px-IMO1985_Problem5.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"435\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9b/IMO1985_Problem5.jpg/1125px-IMO1985_Problem5.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/9b/IMO1985_Problem5.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc051b69921cb1a704265acd6c62c0a96988162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle NKB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_1:_Establishing_the_Initial_Relation\">Step 1: Establishing the Initial Relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f15aafc61e4b27bea583d9f4bdd84e4e015cd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + \\phi = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Step 1: Establishing the Initial Relation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b9f3accb8cef1c55bb4ba5220fde760a8eadbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKNC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the exterior angle at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> equals the interior opposite angle at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e2f90ba4306ca41c78f6a8d5dc6c5c521d206e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle NKB = \\angle ACN = \\theta\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"13\" />\nBy the inscribed angle theorem, the central angle subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is twice the angle on the circumference:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043876b87bda0c49c88dc5f33304d487f9639edb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AON = 2\\angle ACN = 2\\theta\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"13\" />\nConsider the isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750bcc5f6edff4c2a8b44cc4977984a94913f1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbfc94a530ac28911015c68483c5ee1ceed9e328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> (radii of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be the angle such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4beff4026f0f3ad2db2069a81c11fc8d77ba1325.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AON + 2\\phi = 180^\\circ \\implies 2\\theta + 2\\phi = 180^\\circ \\implies \\theta + \\phi = 90^\\circ\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_2:_Tracking_Angles_Subtended_by_Arcs_of_Circle\">Step 2: Tracking Angles Subtended by Arcs of Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Step 2: Tracking Angles Subtended by Arcs of Circle\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the central angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/8224708d8f84fafc8081be491b147441581296f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KON = 2\\eta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. The inscribed angle subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b902cd5392b3e4bbda5878d8ae7f99eb8291eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KN$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ade46e62b4510661185a949c9f0174d93403e60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle NAK = \\eta\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />\nSimilarly, let the inscribed angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08eff1035425c1fd10638cd111dc788e14552e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ANK = \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />, which implies the central angle subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370334b1a3582d54fad42c735dfdded7d216d3cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0e794b28077ede4ee47fa4680e56ba499dee2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOK = 2\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. \nLooking at the exterior angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6c965b26c0edfb31ae0b7b06d48d6fe91cb485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ANK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c681073552daedf49ad7e36967413e85a99d59f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle NKB = \\angle NAK + \\angle ANK \\implies \\theta = \\eta + \\lambda\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_3:_Proving_Quadrilateral_is_Cyclic\">Step 3: Proving Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6793a466c3ba9ecd79fd9a5986b34b3ac7c4b8c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMWN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> is Cyclic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Step 3: Proving Quadrilateral  is Cyclic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb399638caeb905b046637149bd09cd2de45bc57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABM = \\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />. In the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, the angles subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> must be equal:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/142c24d3dd2553a551204de744eb1fe0dba9d5b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ACM = \\angle ABM = \\delta\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"13\" />\nThus, the remaining angle at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1da6f8f2c1cad4e5e8571757ce3e751c654f8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle MCB = \\angle ACN - \\angle ACM = \\theta - \\delta\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"13\" />\nIn the same circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, the angles subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856c130e0bb237c3edeb7e3c0246d40cc607e861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> are equal, which yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da16c7d2729ee1ccd25f6dcde4371bcc4d9b841.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle MAB = \\angle MCB = \\theta - \\delta\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"13\" />\nFrom the properties of the configuration, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b07b81d5cd15203a923817accfa0a5e2b46a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MNW = \\theta - \\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/739f4c0780034a8e67b947389456d9f02fdd8e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MAB = \\angle MNW = \\theta - \\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" /> and both angles subtend the same segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d1b4f880df20c8ed6c129995ed9bd0ec2e294a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MW$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, it follows immediately that <b>quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6793a466c3ba9ecd79fd9a5986b34b3ac7c4b8c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMWN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic</b>. \n</p><p>From this cyclic property, the angles subtending arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> are equal:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d1b5e0f126cea4d4a09ef2f70d8317b6dba3b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AMN = \\angle AWN = 2\\phi\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_4:_Proving_Quadrilateral_is_Cyclic\">Step 4: Proving Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4284c7cb3d253a443f8cbe0bf3438490e2eed7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is Cyclic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Step 4: Proving Quadrilateral  is Cyclic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Now, let us examine the sum of the opposite angles in quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4284c7cb3d253a443f8cbe0bf3438490e2eed7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9c3de7932dfd0e649c33ad0a3a5bf2fa87f74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AON + \\angle AMN = 2\\lambda + 2\\eta + 2\\phi\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"17\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/0690f42d3d7859e4cad1312d60ae299d737e95d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda + \\eta = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> from Step 2 into the equation gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523c8454cbcd31195d18a37dcf011f5ae58f71e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AON + \\angle AMN = 2\\theta + 2\\phi = 2(\\theta + \\phi)\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"18\" />\nUsing our initial relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f15aafc61e4b27bea583d9f4bdd84e4e015cd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + \\phi = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> established in Step 1:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d52af265ef7b9f5e6299f5de28c810015355d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AON + \\angle AMN = 2(90^\\circ) = 180^\\circ\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" />\nSince the opposite angles sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, <b>quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4284c7cb3d253a443f8cbe0bf3438490e2eed7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic</b>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Step_5:_Final_Evaluation\">Step 5: Final Evaluation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Step 5: Final Evaluation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4284c7cb3d253a443f8cbe0bf3438490e2eed7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOMN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral, the angles subtending the same arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb3aa28627d70a5c4421063effb76bd2241a7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> must be equal:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a0f4166f6b925315214eeaa2a4695dba0df381f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle OMN = \\angle OAN = \\phi\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />\nFinally, we evaluate the target angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d2f12f0e595c6a198cc980963de7892f6812a9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43c3d4d0c7ba37f6405835db7600e0789231d78c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle OMB = \\angle OMN + \\angle MNB\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"14\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/4670e2cbf7b031a3d473495a42f45400cf09700e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMN = \\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98cfdb4edab15ece8577002670d3ce457341c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MNB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9830710c8d43968a8fea080a46b66edc961d10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle OMB = \\phi + \\theta = 90^\\circ\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point\" title=\"Miquel&#39;s point\">Miquel's point</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016211206\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.077 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.148 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 904/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30991/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.096      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.096      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7459:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016211206 and revision id 288357. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}